/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 71 0 R
/T (The selected scenario describes an interior-design startup considering a WebXR-based furniture preview. The virtual red velvet chair should look believable in a bright room, the leather sofa should display fine surface detail without requiring a dense mesh, and user input should correspond to the correct screen region. These requirements connect practical retail visualization with illumination models, surface appearance techniques and coordinate transformations.)
/E (The selected scenario describes an interior-design startup considering a WebXR-based furniture preview. The virtual red velvet chair should look believable in a bright room, the leather sofa should display fine surface detail without requiring a dense mesh, and user input should correspond to the correct screen region. These requirements connect practical retail visualization with illumination models, surface appearance techniques and coordinate transformations.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
