184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 72 0 R
/T (A 3D mesh passes through a sequence of operations before appearing on screen. Its vertices are transformed from local space into world and camera space, projected, clipped and rasterized. During rasterization, attributes such as surface normals and UV coordinates are interpolated across triangles. Fragment shading then uses these values to calculate the final surface colour. The Unity example uses a compact forward-shading approach in ShaderLab/HLSL so that the lighting contributions can be inspected directly.)
/E (A 3D mesh passes through a sequence of operations before appearing on screen. Its vertices are transformed from local space into world and camera space, projected, clipped and rasterized. During rasterization, attributes such as surface normals and UV coordinates are interpolated across triangles. Fragment shading then uses these values to calculate the final surface colour. The Unity example uses a compact forward-shading approach in ShaderLab/HLSL so that the lighting contributions can be inspected directly.)
/Pg 14 0 R
