218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 73 0 R
/T (Phong shading is useful for teaching because its ambient, diffuse and specular components are easy to identify. Physically based rendering \(PBR\) uses parameters such as roughness and metallic response, with a stronger emphasis on energy-consistent material behaviour. PBR is generally a better direction for production consistency, while the simpler Phong model is retained here because it directly demonstrates the concepts required by the case study.)
/E (Phong shading is useful for teaching because its ambient, diffuse and specular components are easy to identify. Physically based rendering \(PBR\) uses parameters such as roughness and metallic response, with a stronger emphasis on energy-consistent material behaviour. PBR is generally a better direction for production consistency, while the simpler Phong model is retained here because it directly demonstrates the concepts required by the case study.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
