282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 74 0 R
/T (The Unity controller constructs the room, assigns the custom shader to the furniture and sets up a directional light and simulated ambient environment. Moving the camera changes the view direction and therefore changes the specular response. The demonstration is intended to make the three lighting components understandable. A real AR implementation would also need device-based light estimation, shadow information, exposure handling, occlusion, colour calibration and low interaction latency.)
/E (The Unity controller constructs the room, assigns the custom shader to the furniture and sets up a directional light and simulated ambient environment. Moving the camera changes the view direction and therefore changes the specular response. The demonstration is intended to make the three lighting components understandable. A real AR implementation would also need device-based light estimation, shadow information, exposure handling, occlusion, colour calibration and low interaction latency.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
