/T (When a virtual chair is rendered on a phone, its points are transformed by model, view and projection matrices before viewport mapping. Picking an object from touch input follows the reverse idea: the screen position is converted into a ray or world-space query using camera and projection information. The prototype demonstrates two-dimensional viewport mapping and camera-rectangle changes, but it does not implement AR plane detection or headset gaze selection.)
/E (When a virtual chair is rendered on a phone, its points are transformed by model, view and projection matrices before viewport mapping. Picking an object from touch input follows the reverse idea: the screen position is converted into a ray or world-space query using camera and projection information. The prototype demonstrates two-dimensional viewport mapping and camera-rectangle changes, but it does not implement AR plane detection or headset gaze selection.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [18]
