301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 75 0 R
/T (The procedural pattern is numerically differentiated across neighbouring texture pixels to create a normal texture. The fragment shader decodes the RGB value into a signed vector, scales its tangent-space x and y components using a configurable bump-strength value, and transforms it through the local tangent basis. The resulting normal is used for diffuse and specular calculations. The B key or the material control independently toggles this effect, while the mesh topology remains unchanged.)
/E (The procedural pattern is numerically differentiated across neighbouring texture pixels to create a normal texture. The fragment shader decodes the RGB value into a signed vector, scales its tangent-space x and y components using a configurable bump-strength value, and transforms it through the local tangent basis. The resulting normal is used for diffuse and specular calculations. The B key or the material control independently toggles this effect, while the mesh topology remains unchanged.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
