/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 78 0 R
/T (The Unity project is relatively small, shareable as source code and does not depend on external artwork. Its exposed controls make graphics concepts visible instead of hiding them inside a high-level material preset. Students can compare Phong lighting stages, inspect albedo and normal mapping separately, and verify a known viewport coordinate. This makes the application suitable for a short demonstration and for explaining the mathematical ideas behind the three case-study questions.)
/E (The Unity project is relatively small, shareable as source code and does not depend on external artwork. Its exposed controls make graphics concepts visible instead of hiding them inside a high-level material preset. Students can compare Phong lighting stages, inspect albedo and normal mapping separately, and verify a known viewport coordinate. This makes the application suitable for a short demonstration and for explaining the mathematical ideas behind the three case-study questions.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
