/T (A real AR furniture application would need access to a camera feed or XR compositor, calibration of physical scale, reliable plane detection, occlusion with room objects, consistent shadow estimation and a touch-to-ray interaction process. Furniture models would also need verified dimensions, suitable UV layouts and dependable textures. Mobile browsers introduce further limits involving GPU capacity, memory, device temperature, permissions and screen variation. The current project does not claim to address these deployment requirements.)
/E (A real AR furniture application would need access to a camera feed or XR compositor, calibration of physical scale, reliable plane detection, occlusion with room objects, consistent shadow estimation and a touch-to-ray interaction process. Furniture models would also need verified dimensions, suitable UV layouts and dependable textures. Mobile browsers introduce further limits involving GPU capacity, memory, device temperature, permissions and screen variation. The current project does not claim to address these deployment requirements.)
