/Title (When the application starts, the controller creates primitive furniture geometry, applies the custom shader, generates procedural leather textures, adds a directional light and configures the camera. During each frame, input handling updates the selected lighting mode, focused object, camera orbit and material switches. Vertex processing transforms the mesh, while fragment processing evaluates the texture samples, perturbed normals and lighting terms. The camera then displays the rendered scene in the active Game viewport, and the interface presents the related controls.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 900 0 R
>>
endobj
