988 0 obj
<<
/Title (The procedural pattern is numerically differentiated across neighbouring texture pixels to create a normal texture. The fragment shader decodes the RGB value into a signed vector, scales its tangent-space x and y components using a configurable bump-strength value, and transforms it through the local tangent basis. The resulting normal is used for diffuse and specular calculations. The B key or the material control independently toggles this effect, while the mesh topology remains unchanged.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 972 0 R
>>
endobj
