1011 0 obj
<<
/Title (Bump mapping simulates small changes in surface orientation, while normal mapping stores those directions more directly. A tangent-space normal map stores x, y and z components in RGB channels. The shader converts the stored values from the [0,1] range into signed vector components, then uses a tangent-bitangent-normal \(TBN\) basis to transform the vector into world space. The resulting perturbed normal affects diffuse and specular shading, creating the appearance of pores and creases without changing the mesh boundaries.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1005 0 R
/Next 1021 0 R
>>
endobj
