/Title (The chair and sofa use RGB colours and textures. The final displayed colour is influenced by display transfer functions and the rendering colour space. A production renderer may perform lighting in linear space and treat image textures as sRGB data to improve colour compositing. The teaching shader clarifies lighting contributions, but it is not a calibrated system for reproducing the exact colour of real fabric. Consequently, the same red chair may appear different on different displays.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1016 0 R
>>
endobj
1028 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ambient illumination prevents areas outside direct light from becoming completely black. It can be represented as the surface albedo multiplied by an ambient-strength value. A modest level helps the chair remain readable in the showroom. In a real AR system, this value should be estimated from the surrounding environment rather than chosen arbitrarily.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1018 0 R
>>
endobj
